	(text "The pot side of the chip (U2A) is drawn on the Audio sheet.\nV+ = 9V and V- = GND, so the pot ends can swing anywhere from 0V to 9V.\nVL = 3.3V matches the microcontroller's logic.  WLAT tied low: a new setting takes effect at once.\nSHDN tied high: normal operation.  At power-up the wiper starts at mid-scale (about +15 dB)\nuntil the microcontroller restores the saved setting; the bypass relay is still off then.\n\nNote: the datasheet specifies the analog side from V+ = 10V.  At about 8.6V it still works\n(it resets below 6V) but the wiper resistance is higher: about 150 ohms instead of 75.\nThat sets the minimum Boost (+1 dB).  Confirm on the breadboard, along with the pot's\ndistortion in a clean signal, the main open question for this pedal."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 114.3 101.6 0)
		(effects (font (size 1 1)) (justify left))
		(uuid "39c00534-4289-4b26-8c2e-7ae26589f2cf")
	)
